    "AI Notes": {
      "value": "Interdisciplinary Kenyan/Trinidadian-American artist (b. 1993), based Washington DC, US. Painting, pattern/textile design and illustration exploring Black identity and diaspora; kanga-inspired patterns. BFA Parsons 2016. Gallery-exhibited (Hamiltonian, Mehari Sequar) plus commercial clients: Dior, Penguin Random House, Meta, Spotify, Chronicle Books. ~10 yrs practice, mid-career, exhibits and sells as an artist. Freelance/independent artist: own site + LinkedIn + press agree. Autonomy 4 (inferred): runs her own studio practice and delivers to commission. Tagged Illustration only; her work reads strongly as Art practice (and Graphic design for pattern/textile), see Open Questions. IG handle @vivaillajams on entry is dead/deleted; current active account confirmed as @jamillaokubo (Jamilla Okubo Studio, 17.8K followers, June 2026). Website jamillaokubo.co is a placeholder; best context at hamiltonianartists.org/resident-artists/jamilla-okubo/.",
